            <ArticleTitle>A solution to the problem of an unexpanded Palmaz-Schatz stent following balloon rupture.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>246-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Palmaz-Schatz stent is a balloon expandable stent. Although easy to deploy, problems can occur. One problem is balloon rupture resulting in a partially expanded stent, which can be difficult to expand fully. This report illustrates how a Probing catheter and balloon can solve this potentially serious problem.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
